WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:06.395
The escape pod shot through space.

2
00:00:06.396 --> 00:00:09.734
Ally kept trying to turn it around, but nothing worked.

3
00:00:09.735 --> 00:00:12.411
Then suddenly things got worse.

4
00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:16.020
"Warning: low fuel," the computer said.

5
00:00:16.021 --> 00:00:18.134
"How low?" Ally snapped.

6
00:00:18.135 --> 00:00:20.340
"Must land to refuel."

7
00:00:20.341 --> 00:00:24.893
"Are you kidding me?" Ally groaned.

8
00:00:24.894 --> 00:00:30.330
"Where's the closest planet to refuel—and get parts to fix the comm device?"

9
00:00:30.331 --> 00:00:33.792
The computer whirred.

10
00:00:33.793 --> 00:00:37.988
"Nearest planet with intelligent life is Earth.

11
00:00:37.989 --> 00:00:43.522
Atmosphere: oxygen. Dominant life-form: human, also called Earthling.

12
00:00:43.523 --> 00:00:49.103
Temperament: intelligent, creative, sometimes friendly but often dangerous.

13
00:00:49.104 --> 00:00:55.045
Previous attempts to make contact with humans: unsuccessful. Deemed too dangerous."

14
00:00:55.046 --> 00:00:58.993
Ally gulped. "Dangerous?"

15
00:00:58.994 --> 00:01:02.615
"Some humans are curious about visitors from other realms.

16
00:01:02.616 --> 00:01:06.679
But most are suspicious and respond with aggression."

17
00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:12.857
"Yikes!" Ally had never heard of a life-form that didn't treat Astralians with deep respect. "Engage

18
00:01:12.858 --> 00:01:18.026
meld medallion to activate human-shaped camouflage for protection." "Phew!"

19
00:01:18.027 --> 00:01:23.417
Ally said. "I can camouflage myself to look like a human. Okay,

20
00:01:23.418 --> 00:01:29.239
Alpha, let's land on Earth." Ally

21
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:33.786
watched as the pod approached the pretty blue-and-green planet. "Earth

22
00:01:33.787 --> 00:01:45.195
matches my outfit," she thought. "It can't be too bad." The

23
00:01:45.196 --> 00:01:55.524
pod flew low over a deserted sandy area before touching down behind some trees in a park. Ally

24
00:01:55.525 --> 00:02:01.697
slipped on her meld medallion, a necklace that contained special technology. It

25
00:02:01.698 --> 00:02:04.598
allowed her to blend in with other life-forms. She

26
00:02:04.599 --> 00:02:11.106
expected to feel different instantly, but instead she felt just like herself—until she looked in the mirror. "Wow!"

27
00:02:11.107 --> 00:02:19.469
Her tentacles had been transformed into red, curly hair, and her nose was now sharp and pointy. But

28
00:02:19.470 --> 00:02:23.441
the most surprising change was to her feet. "Ugh

29
00:02:23.442 --> 00:02:27.024
. . . My feet look so small now." "Small

30
00:02:27.025 --> 00:02:31.045
feet are the least of your problems," the computer said. Ally

31
00:02:31.046 --> 00:02:38.360
ignored the comment and went outside. She

32
00:02:38.361 --> 00:02:43.466
used her meld medallion to shrink the pod and camouflage it among the trees. "Don't

33
00:02:43.467 --> 00:02:52.938
go anywhere, Alpha. I might need to escape quickly from this place!" As

34
00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:58.939
she stepped out from behind the trees, Ally saw some posters about local attractions along the path. Two

35
00:02:58.940 --> 00:03:03.388
humans—a mother and daughter—were looking at one of the posters. Ally

36
00:03:03.389 --> 00:03:06.723
tried to read their minds but couldn't hear anything. "Hmm,"

37
00:03:06.724 --> 00:03:12.598
she thought. "Maybe my mind-reading ability doesn't work here." She

38
00:03:12.599 --> 00:03:17.538
lifted her arms in a traditional Astralian greeting. "Hello!" The little

39
00:03:17.539 --> 00:03:26.431
girl spun around. "An alien, Mommy! A real one!" Ally froze.

40
00:03:26.432 --> 00:03:32.331
But the

41
00:03:32.332 --> 00:03:44.085
mother smiled. "That's just a friendly teenager, honey. Wave and say hello!" After the

42
00:03:44.086 --> 00:03:48.757
humans walked away, Ally went over to look at the posters. One showed

43
00:03:48.758 --> 00:03:54.621
a picture of a large glass building—with a GrayZonian spaceship floating above it. Intrigued, Ally

44
00:03:54.622 --> 00:03:58.852
held up her meld medallion to translate the poster. It read,

45
00:03:58.853 --> 00:04:04.989
"Visit the World-Famous Sandville UFO Museum!" "That sounds

46
00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:10.681
like the perfect place to find parts and fuel," Ally thought. *** After

47
00:04:10.682 --> 00:04:14.889
walking around for thirty minutes, Ally still hadn't found the museum. She'd

48
00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:22.018
been on hot planets before, but this one seemed particularly warm with a blazing sun and no clouds. She

49
00:04:22.019 --> 00:04:28.784
felt hot and hungry. Just

50
00:04:28.785 --> 00:04:32.400
then she caught a delicious scent. "Food!"

51
00:04:32.401 --> 00:04:43.225
She jumped up and followed the scent to a busy street with a crowded restaurant. A

52
00:04:43.226 --> 00:04:50.096
sign read, "Pepe's Diner. Grand Opening Today!" Ally

53
00:04:50.097 --> 00:04:57.314
took a deep breath and went inside. To

54
